<title>USA: Ahmanson sees Q2 charge for merger costs.</title>
<headline>Ahmanson sees Q2 charge for merger costs.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>H.F. Ahmanson and Co said it expects to take a second quarter charge for costs related to its unsuccessful bid for Great Western Financial Corp.</p>
<p>A spokeswoman would not disclose the size of the charge.</p>
<p>In the year-ago second quarter, Ahmanson reported net income of 68.7 million and $0.50 per share on a fully diluted basis.</p>
<p>Ahmanson withdrew its $6.73 billion hostile bid Wednesday after a Delaware court Tuesday denied its request to delay a June 13 vote on a friendly agreement between Great Western and Washington Mutual Inc.</p>
</text>
